    "ages": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "text": "Which is better for your child's age?",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "heading_tag_html": "h2",
            "text_color": "",
            "gradient": ""
          }
        },
        "body": {
          "type": "richtext",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p><strong>1 to 3 years.</strong> The Toniebox is the easier fit. The soft box takes knocks, you squeeze an ear to change the volume, and the figures are part of the fun. Yoto and Voxblock are made for children from 3.</p><p><strong>3 to 7 years.</strong> All three work. Tonies suit children who still play with the figures; Yoto suits families who want lots of content and a bedside clock; Voxblock suits families who want no wi-fi and stories children keep on a shelf.</p><p><strong>7 and older.</strong> Yoto or Voxblock. Both carry longer chapter books; Voxblock has unabridged novels for older children. Most Tonies content is aimed at younger listeners.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
