    "faq": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "item_1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Yoto or Tonies: which is better?",
            "content": "<p>Neither is better for every child. A Toniebox suits toddlers who love figures; a Yoto suits children from 3 who want more stories and lasts further into the school years.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What age is a Toniebox for?",
            "content": "<p>Tonies is aimed at the youngest listeners, from around 1 to 5. Most families move on as children start chapter books.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Do Yoto and Tonies need wi-fi?",
            "content": "<p>Both need wi-fi and an app to set up. Each new Tonie downloads when it is first played; Yoto cards load their audio over wi-fi. Voxblock needs neither.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_4": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Which is cheaper, Yoto or Tonies?",
            "content": "<p>The Yoto Mini (£89.99) costs less than the Toniebox 2 (£104.99), and Yoto cards (£7.99) cost about half a Tonie (£14.99).</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_5": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can you use wired headphones with a Toniebox?",
            "content": "<p>No. The Toniebox 2 has Bluetooth only. Yoto players have a 3.5mm jack and Bluetooth; Voxblock has a 3.5mm jack.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
